      "message": "Low: the guard is a bare truthiness test. An empty string is correctly treated as unset, but a whitespace-only value (e.g. \" \") passes the guard and renders \u0027default_volume_type \u003d \u0027 with a blank value, which Cinder would reject or misinterpret at service start — a mis-typed manifest value silently produces a broken config line instead of falling back to __DEFAULT__.\n\nSuggested fix: normalize before rendering, e.g. {% set dvt \u003d options.default_volume_type | trim -%} then guard and render dvt; or validate the option in config-changed. Also consider a unit test for the empty-string config value to pin the \u0027unset behaves like absent\u0027 behavior.",
      "revId": "e149f4cbcc8c330c0c35552578d875b86d7bea6f",
